{
  "_comment": [
    "Award requirements. EDIT THIS FILE to retune; rebuild and redeploy to apply.",
    "",
    "TITLES are operator policy. Nothing in the game states a threshold -- the client's own",
    "descriptions name the statistic ('High kill count') and never the number. The values here come",
    "from a community requirements list for a LATE version of MGO2, adapted to the 22 titles this",
    "disc ships, with gaps filled by best guess. They are expected to be wrong in places and are",
    "meant to be edited. See dev/docs/AWARDS.md for the sources and their disagreements.",
    "",
    "MEDALS are different: the 'value' is the number the client PRINTS in that medal's own caption,",
    "so awarding at exactly that number is what makes the screen truthful. Change these only if you",
    "want the screen to state a requirement you did not apply.",
    "",
    "A clause is {metric, op, value} plus an optional 'modes' filter. Metrics are a fixed set",
    "implemented in AwardMetric.java -- this file chooses among them, it cannot define new ones.",
    "All clauses of a title must pass. 'rank' orders titles for the displayed one: LOWEST rank wins.",
    "'bit' is the position in the 22-bit mask at 0x4103 wire 563 and MUST be 0..21 -- bit 22 or above",
    "corrupts the client's scrollbar.",
    "",
    "Modes: DM TDM RES CAP SNE BASE. TSNE exists on the disc but is never played (release-day scope),",
    "so CHAMELEON can never be earned; it is kept so it works the day rule 7 is enabled."
  ],

